  "domain": "spatial-computing",
  "definition": "A per-vertex data channel attached to the vertices of a polygon mesh \u2014 position, normal, tangent, texture coordinates, colour, skinning joint indices and weights \u2014 supplied to the vertex shader as its input. Attributes are stored in vertex buffers with a declared layout (location, format, offset, stride), interpolated across triangles during rasterisation for per-pixel shading, and standardised by interchange formats such as glTF, making them the fundamental unit of geometry data throughout the graphics pipeline.",
